# LLM-GC's own key, used only by LLM-GC and never for your conversation with Claude.
#
# LLM-GC calls a model itself, briefly, to summarise old exchanges and read their facts.
# This key pays for those calls alone. Your conversation keeps using your client's own
# login (Claude Code's, for one), which LLM-GC passes on and never stores. The model for
# LLM-GC's calls is chosen separately too, as `model` under [summary] in llm-gc.toml.
#
# Copy this file to .env (git-ignored), then fill in ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN below, whichever your setup uses. `llm-gc` reads .env from the folder
# you start it in. A line left as `NAME=` counts as not set.
#
# To check it, run `llm-gc config show`: its last line says whether LLM-GC has a key.

# Direct setup: an API key from console.anthropic.com. A Claude Pro or Max subscription
# doesn't include one; the Console bills it separately.
# Gateway setup: if ~/.claude/settings.json has ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, copy its value here. Sent as x-api-key.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Gateway setup: if ~/.claude/settings.json has ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN, copy its value here.
# Sent as Authorization: Bearer.
ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Only when LLM-GC summarises with OpenAI (`provider = "openai"` under [summary]).
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Other settings belong in llm-gc.toml, which `llm-gc config init` writes. Any of them can
# also be set here as LLM_GC_<NAME> (for example LLM_GC_LOG_LEVEL=DEBUG); the README's
# Configuration section lists them all.
